    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, even if you only reveal one of the applicable cards, you can still add it to your hand.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards I reveal from my deck for this card's effect include only either a card with the [Hybrid] or [Ten Warriors] trait or a Tamer card with an inherited effect, can I just add that 1 card to my hand?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. If you have cards that are targets of this effect, you must add as many cards to your hand as possible.",
        "question": "If the 3 cards I reveal from my deck for this card's effect include both a card with the [Hybrid] or [Ten Warriors] trait and a Tamer card with an inherited effect, can I choose to only add one of them to my hand, and place the remaining cards at the bottom of my deck?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "It means a Tamer card with \"Inherited Effect\" in its lower text.  A Tamer card with a [Security] effect in its lower text isn't a \"Tamer card with inherited effects.\"",
